  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Occupational Therapy Assistant A.S. Degree - (OTA) Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 3, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7635/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local. Official Total Units: 79-82; this seed models the path consistent with the map's printed semester headers = 13+15+14+14.5+8+10.5+6 = 81 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). TERM MERGE NOTE: the official map spans 9 terms (Semesters 1-7 plus two Summer Sessions across four years). Because the shared validator caps associate plans at 7 terms, the two Summer Sessions are merged into the preceding Spring semesters and clearly labeled: Semester 4 = official Semester 4 (Spring, 10 units) + Summer Session (4.5 units); Semester 6 = official Semester 6 (Spring, 9 units) + Summer Session (1.5 units). Within each merged term, complete the Spring courses before the Summer courses (the map's official sequence is preserved in course order). IMPORTANT BIOLOGY PATH NOTE: the map offers 'BIOL 302 (1 semester) OR BIOL 430 & BIOL 431 (2 semesters after completing CHEM 305)' and states BIOL 302 is the department-recommended course. However, the map's printed semester totals (Semester 2: 13-15, Semester 3: 14 including BIOL 431 at 5 units) and the official 79-82 total are computed on the BIOL 430 -> BIOL 431 path. This seed therefore models BIOL 430 (Semester 2, 5 units — the value consistent with the printed 13-15 header) followed by BIOL 431 (Semester 3, 5 units). Students who complete the recommended BIOL 302 instead skip BIOL 431 in Semester 3, which lowers the total below the printed range. BIOL 430 requires completion of CHEM 305, 309 or 400 with 'C' or better (prior coursework, not in this map — see a counselor). BIOL 431 requires BIOL 430 with 'C' or better (in-plan). Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 / ENGL 488 / ESLW 340 (Honors), Area L1A; (2) NUTRI 300 / NUTRI 480 (Honors), Area L5; (3) PSYC 370 / EDUC 300; (4) STAT C1000 / STAT C1000H, Area L2; (5) OTA 132 / OTA 122 (Semester 4 — OTA 132 selected; OTA 122 requires AH 106 with 'C' or better); (6) OTA 142 / OTA 122 (Semester 5 — OTA 142 selected). Same-semester corequisites (documented, not in prereq arrays): OTA 131 <-> OTA 132; OTA 110 <-> OTA 111; OTA 140 <-> OTA 141 <-> OTA 142; OTA 160 <-> OTA 162; OTA 161 <-> OTA 163. Placement prereqs (documented, not in prereq arrays): students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take the STAT 10/STAT C1000 combo. Program eligibility: students are eligible to apply for the OTA program after completing all prerequisite and GE courses (after Semester 3); financial-aid students must claim PRE-HEALTH OCCUPATIONS as their major until accepted; there may be a waiting period between applying and enrolling in Semester 4. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units, 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, SCC Local GE Areas L1A-L6 with 2.0 GPA. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
